From: FP6 feature-push (battery agent)
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: report charge-control write
 errors; 100 % end threshold disables the limit

Two issues in the charge-control thresholds (seen while adding the FP6
charge limit on kernel6, 7.2.0-fp6-nixos6):

 * qcom_battmgr_set_charge_start_threshold() and
   qcom_battmgr_set_charge_end_threshold() always return 0. A failed
   BATTMGR_CHG_CTRL_LIMIT_EN request (GLINK down, firmware -EIO) is silently
   reported to userspace as success; only the cached values stay stale.
   Return the request's result.

 * Every write sends enable = 1. There is no way back to the firmware's boot
   state (enable = 0; on FP6 it reports 70/80 but charges to 100 %): writing
   100 becomes "limit 100 % with recharge below 100 - delta". Treat an end
   threshold of 100 % (CHARGE_CTRL_END_THR_MAX) as "no limit" and send
   enable = 0.

Applies on top of ../misc/0001-power-supply-qcom_battmgr-report-charge-in-uAh-on-SM8350-family.patch
(kernel6 order). NOT built into kernel6 (pinned). Userspace (fp6-batteryd)
works without it: it never writes before a limit is chosen and verifies
every write by readback.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -666,11 +666,16 @@
 static int qcom_battmgr_set_charge_control(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
 					   u32 target_soc, u32 delta_soc)
 {
+	/*
+	 * An end threshold of 100 % is no limit: send enable = 0, which is the
+	 * firmware's own boot state, instead of a 100 % "limit" with a delta.
+	 */
+	bool enable = target_soc < CHARGE_CTRL_END_THR_MAX;
 	struct qcom_battmgr_charge_ctrl_request request = {
 		.hdr.owner = cpu_to_le32(PMIC_GLINK_OWNER_BATTMGR),
 		.hdr.type = cpu_to_le32(PMIC_GLINK_REQ_RESP),
 		.hdr.opcode = cpu_to_le32(BATTMGR_CHG_CTRL_LIMIT_EN),
-		.enable = cpu_to_le32(1),
+		.enable = cpu_to_le32(enable),
 		.target_soc = cpu_to_le32(target_soc),
 		.delta_soc = cpu_to_le32(delta_soc),
 	};
@@ -708,7 +713,7 @@
 		battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_end = target_soc;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_battmgr_set_charge_end_threshold(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr, int end_soc)
@@ -729,7 +734,7 @@
 		battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_end = end_soc;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_battmgr_charge_control_thresholds_init(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
